g ≤ 100 and queue times; adjust chat‑to‑call ratios on‑the‑fly.\n\n3. **Activate playbooks**  \n   - **Mortgage Inquiry Overflow Playbook** – East, 11:00‑14:00.  \n   - **Dispute Queue Surge Playbook** – both regions, anytime dispute cases rise >20 %.\n\n4. **Back‑up mentor pool** – reserve ≥10 % of mentors for dispute spikes; monitor usage logs.\n\n5. **Post‑shift simulation** – if East backlog >100, revisit temp staffing for next day.  \n\n6. **10 % buffer usage** – treat as the last line of defense; if breached, trigger overtime/shift‑overlap review.\n\n### Escalation Points\n\n| Condition | Immediate Action |\n|-----------|------------------|\n| East backlog > 100 in peak | Supervisor pulls temps off‑peak; consider adding 1 more temp next day. |\n| Central backlog > 90 in peak | Re‑allocate chat agents to calls; add extra temp if trend persists. |\n| Dispute volume > 20 % surge | Deploy backup mentors; activate Dispute Queue Surge Playbook; inform product team. |\n| Overtime / break limits breached | Alert shift manager; explore shift overlap or next‑day re‑forecast. |\n\n### Service Risk Summary\n\n- **High East backlog** → potential SLA breach (≥30 min hold).  \n- **Central near‑threshold backlog** → risk of queue spikes in absence of over‑assignment.  \n- **Unpredictable dispute surge** → possible depletion of back‑up mentors.  \n- **Fixed 8‑hr roster** → limited flexibility; no overtime or cross‑shift coverage.  \n- **10 % buffer loss** → may trigger hold time increase.  \n- **Backlog carry‑over** → uneven agent utilisation day‑to‑day.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Conclusion\n\n- **Overall staffing**: 62 agents effectively across two regions (validated), with additional temp coverage at peak windows.  \n- **Risk mitigations** are in place through supervisors, playbooks, and backup mentors.  \n- **Schedule ID**: **SCH‑5F157B96** – use this for reporting and post‑shift analysis.  \n\nMaintain monitoring dashboards for backlog, hold times, and SLA compliance. Adjust next‑day forecast if East’s backlog remains >100 or Central’s close to threshold."
